F326                             ; ---- reached from a handler ------------------------------------------------
F326                             ; chkst: stop with O unless X is in the program's own space: from the letter
F326                             ; page up to HEAPLIM, so the interpreter's stacks and whatever lies above the
F326                             ; limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but below the limit is the
F326                             ; program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there. Keeps every register.
F326   8C 82 00     CHKST:    CMPX   #LET   
F329   25 06                  BLO   cs9   
F32B   8C EF 00               CMPX   #HEAPLIM*256   
F32E   24 01                  BHS   cs9   
F330   39                     RTS      ; in range
