F339                             ; and fall into error. (H, W and N have their own entries, near
F339                             ; their handlers, at ejmp.)
F339                             ; =============================================================================
F339                             ;  Checked build: the error report. A = the letter, AT = the place; U is
F339                             ;  as the program left it, and SSAV holds S as the failing character began
F339                             ;  (see "the error entries" after `upper`).
F339                             ;  It sits here, ahead of h_num, pdec and putc, so that it reaches them with
F339                             ;  short calls. Prints
F339                             ; 
F339                             ;     CR LF
F339                             ;     Err X @ line,col CR LF
F339                             ;     D:n:[ ...][ v]*  CR LF     (the top 8 cells, bottom to top, signed)
F339                             ;     R:n CR LF
F339                             ; 
F339                             ;  and goes to EXIT. Line and column count from 1: the line is one more
F339                             ;  than the LFs between PROG and the place, the column the distance from the
F339                             ;  last LF (or from PROG-1). A place below PROG is in the -n? line buffer:
F339                             ;  line 0, column = its offset there + 1. Numbers other than the cells are
F339                             ;  printed unsigned (pdec), the cells signed (h_num).
F339                             ; 
F339                             ;  The data stack may be one cell past its limit (S, U = 8100h): the
F339                             ;  report's own cells then reach 6 bytes further down, to 80FAh, into the
F339                             ;  return stack page, so the report runs on a fresh return stack at RSREP
F339                             ;  (80F0h), below those bytes.
F339                             ; =============================================================================
F339   10 CE 80 F0  ERROR:    LDS   #RSREP   
F33D   1F 89                  TFR   A,B   ; the letter (pmsg and CONOUT keep B)
F33F   8D 34                  BSR   pmsg   
F341   0D 0A 45 72 72 A0      FCB   13,10,"Err"," "+80h   
F347   1F 98                  TFR   B,A   
F349   BD FF 03               JSR   CONOUT   
F34C   8D 27                  BSR   pmsg   
F34E   20 40 A0               FCB   " @"," "+80h   
F351                             ; the place: Y counts the lines, X walks, the cell at ,U holds the
F351                             ; address of the last LF (PROG-1 to begin with)
F351   10 8E 00 00            LDY   #0   
F355   8E 82 7F               LDX   #LINEBUF-1   
F358   36 10                  PSHU   X   
F35A   8E 82 FF               LDX   #PROG-1   
F35D   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F35F   24 23                  BHS   lc3   ; the place is below PROG: line 0
F361   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F363   31 21        LC1:      LEAY   1,Y   ; a line
F365   30 01        LC2:      LEAX   1,X   
F367   9C 36                  CMPX   <AT   
F369   24 19                  BHS   lc3   
F36B   A6 84                  LDA   ,X   
F36D   81 0A                  CMPA   #10   
F36F   26 F4                  BNE   lc2   
F371   AF C4                  STX   ,U   
F373   20 EE                  BRA   lc1   
F375                             ; pmsg: print the text after the call, up to and including the character
F375                             ; that has bit 7 set (it is printed without it), then return after it.
F375                             ; (It sits here, in the middle of the report, where all its calls reach.)
F375   35 10        PMSG:     PULS   X   
F377   A6 84        PM1:      LDA   ,X   
F379   84 7F                  ANDA   #7Fh   
F37B   BD F4 08               JSR   putc   
F37E   6D 80                  TST   ,X+   
F380   2A F5                  BPL   pm1   
F382   6E 84                  JMP   ,X   
F384   DC 36        LC3:      LDD   <AT   
F386   A3 C4                  SUBD   ,U   
F388   ED C4                  STD   ,U   ; the column
F38A   36 20                  PSHU   Y   
F38C   8D 62                  BSR   pdec   ; the line
F38E   8D E5                  BSR   pmsg   
F390   AC                     FCB   ","+80h   
F391   8D 5D                  BSR   pdec   ; the column
F393   8D E0                  BSR   pmsg   
F395   0D 0A 44 BA            FCB   13,10,"D",":"+80h   
F399                             ; the data stack: its depth, then its top 8 cells, from Y down to
F399                             ; the program's top cell, at ,U.
F399   34 40                  PSHS   U   ; where the walk ends
F39B   CC 81 FC               LDD   #DSTOP   
F39E   A3 E4                  SUBD   ,S   
F3A0   8D 3D                  BSR   pdh   ; the depth (pdec leaves U as it was)
F3A2   8D D1                  BSR   pmsg   
F3A4   BA                     FCB   ":"+80h   
F3A5   31 C8 10               LEAY   16,U   ; past the 8th cell from the top ...
F3A8   10 8C 81 FC            CMPY   #DSTOP   
F3AC   24 08                  BHS   sl1   
F3AE   8D C5                  BSR   pmsg   ; (there are more than 8)
F3B0   20 2E 2E AE            FCB   " ..","."+80h   
F3B4   20 04                  BRA   sl2   
F3B6   10 8E 81 FC  SL1:      LDY   #DSTOP   ; ... or the whole stack, if no more than 8
F3BA   10 AC E4     SL2:      CMPY   ,S   
F3BD   23 0B                  BLS   sl9   
F3BF   EC A3                  LDD   ,--Y   
F3C1   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3C3   8D B0                  BSR   pmsg   
F3C5   A0                     FCB   " "+80h   
F3C6   8D 1D                  BSR   h_num   
F3C8   20 F0                  BRA   sl2   
F3CA   8D A9        SL9:      BSR   pmsg   
F3CC   0D 0A 52 BA            FCB   13,10,"R",":"+80h   
F3D0   CC 81 00               LDD   #RSTOP   ; the return stack's depth, (RSTOP - S) / 2,
F3D3   93 3A                  SUBD   <SSAV   ;   S as it was when this character began
F3D5   8D 08                  BSR   pdh   
F3D7   BD F3 75               JSR   pmsg   
F3DA   0D 8A                  FCB   13,10+80h   
F3DC   7E FF 09               JMP   EXIT   
F3DF                             ; pdh: print D/2 (a depth: D is twice it), unsigned.
F3DF   44           PDH:      LSRA      
F3E0   56                     RORB      
F3E1   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3E3   20 0B                  BRA   pdec   
F3E5                          ENDIF      
F3E5                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
F3E5   6D C4        H_NUM:    TST   ,U   
F3E7   2A 07                  BPL   pdec   
F3E9   86 2D                  LDA   #"-"   
F3EB   8D 1B                  BSR   putc   
F3ED                          IF   CHECKED   
F3ED   17 00 88               LBSR   negt   ; (long: the checked h_print is in between)
F3F0                          ENDIF      
F3F0                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              BSR   negt   
F3F0                          ENDIF      
F3F0                             ; pdec: print the top cell as unsigned and drop it, by recursion on /10
F3F0   CC 00 0A     PDEC:     LDD   #10   
F3F3   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F3F5                          IF   (1-CHECKED)*(1-QK)   
                              BSR   udiv   ; NOS = quotient, TOS = digit
F3F5                          ENDIF      
F3F5                          IF   CHECKED*(1-QK)   
                              LBSR   udiv   ; (out of a BSR's reach here)
F3F5                          ENDIF      
F3F5                          IF   SBASEU   
                              BSR   ud0   ; (base: past the power-of-two test)
F3F5                          ENDIF      
F3F5                          IF   QK-SBASEU   
F3F5   17 00 8F               LBSR   ud0   
F3F8                          ENDIF      
F3F8   37 06                  PULU   D   ; the digit
F3FA   34 04                  PSHS   B   
F3FC   EC C1                  LDD   ,U++   ; the quotient: if it is not 0, it goes
F3FE   27 04                  BEQ   pd1   ;   back for the rest of the digits
F400   36 06                  PSHU   D   
F402   8D EC                  BSR   pdec   
F404   35 02        PD1:      PULS   A   
F406   8B 30                  ADDA   #"0"   ; and fall into putc
F408   7E FF 03     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   
F40B                             ; ---- the tail ---------------------------------------------------------------
F40B                             ; "$" is the last handler, so what follows its first byte may lie past the
F40B                             ; second range: its loop, the escapes, and the routines of "/".
F40B                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
F40B                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
F40B                             ; of a. Unchecked, dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; checked,
F40B                             ; it stops with Z, both operands still on the stack.
F40B                H_DIV:       
F40B                          IF   CHECKED   
F40B   EC C4                  LDD   ,U   
F40D   10 27 FF 23            LBEQ   e_zero   
F411                          ENDIF      
F411   A6 42                  LDA   2,U   
F413   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a's sign: for r
F415   A8 C4                  EORA   ,U   
F417   34 02                  PSHS   A   ; a xor b: for q
F419   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F41B   8D 64                  BSR   absx   ; |a|
F41D   1F 31                  TFR   U,X   
F41F   8D 60                  BSR   absx   ; |b|
F421                          IF   1-QK   
                              BSR   udiv   ; NOS = q, TOS = r
F421                          ENDIF      
F421                          IF   QK   
F421   BD F5 27               JSR   udiv   ; (base: with the speed-ups)
F424                          ENDIF      
F424   30 42                  LEAX   2,U   
F426   6D E0                  TST   ,S+   
F428   2A 02                  BPL   dv1   
F42A   8D 4E                  BSR   negx   ; q's sign
F42C   6D E0        DV1:      TST   ,S+   
F42E   2A 50                  BPL   ng9   
F430   20 46                  BRA   negt   ; r's sign
F432                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character from
F432                             ; 60h to 7Eh is one of the escapes at pesc; "/" plus any other character
F432                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, "/" and DEL is "?"; "/", ""'
F432                             ; and "?" have no bit 6, so //, /" and /? give themselves). The address
F432                             ; comes off the stack first, and Y walks the string (the IP waits on S), so
F432                             ; that /~ finds its row and column on top, and an escape may use A, B, X
F432                             ; and the routines.
F432                             ; Checked: a NUL (not one escaped by "/") stops with Q, the string's
F432                             ; address put back on the stack (from PSAV) over what any /~ left.
F432   34 20        H_PRINT:   PSHS   Y   
F434   37 20                  PULU   Y   
F436                          IF   CHECKED   
F436   11 83 81 FC            CMPU   #DSTOP   ; "$" with nothing on the stack: s, before it
F43A   10 22 FC 56            LBHI   e_ds   ;   prints from an address of no meaning (N
F43E   10 9F 3C               STY   <PSAV   ;   is clear: an underflow)
F441                          ENDIF      
